  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FOJO Southeast Asia Media Training Network</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">FOJO Southeast Asia Media Training Network</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fojo Media Institute has applied to Sida for funding of SEK 20,870,000  for &#x2018;The Southeast Asia Media Training Network&#x2019;, 2015-2018&#x2019;.

The intervention aims at contributing to a professional and independent media sector in Mekong countries by establishing a regional network of journalism training institutions supporting media freedom, freedom of expression and the right to information. The Specific Objective is to strengthen the capacity of mid-career journalism training institutes in a regional network covering initially Myanmar, Vietnam, Laos and Cambodia.

The immediate outcomes of the project are:
&#x2022;	Network members manage their mid-career training institutes more efficiently and effectively
&#x2022;	Network members offer systematic, high-quality mid-career training to media practitioners in the region, meeting contemporary needs of the media industry.
&#x2022;	A regional network established, functioning as a mechanism for peer-to-peer learning and regional cooperation, including partners from Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam.
&#x2022;	Management of network members have increased understanding for the significance of regional and cross-border reporting on issues of regional relevance, such as environment and climate change, HIV/AIDS, gender equality.

Fojo Media Institute will implement the intervention together with ten national and regional media organizations. 

Sweden is the only donor, however, Fojo will be advised to entice more funding agencies to take part in this.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Fojos projektf&#xF6;rslag &#x201C;South East Asia Media Training Network, 1 september 2016 till 30 september 2019, avser en beg&#xE4;ran om st&#xF6;d om 20 870 000 SEK.

Insatsens fokus ligger p&#xE5; att etablera utbyten och utveckla kapacitet inom ett n&#xE4;tverk best&#xE5;ende av institutioner som utbildar journalister i mitten av sina karri&#xE4;rer i Kambodja, Laos, Myanmar och Vietnam. Projektf&#xF6;rslaget bed&#xF6;ms vara relevant f&#xF6;r situationen i regionen, d&#xE4;r det r&#xE5;der brist p&#xE5; initiativ f&#xF6;r vidareutbildning f&#xF6;r journalister. De organisationer och institut som finns jobbar oftast avskilt, med begr&#xE4;nsad tillg&#xE5;ng till regionala och internationella n&#xE4;tverk eller utvecklingsst&#xF6;d. De saknar plattformar f&#xF6;r kunskaps- och erfarenhetsutbyten f&#xF6;r att kunna utveckla egen kapacitet f&#xF6;r fr&#xE4;mjande av journalism och media. Det saknas kvalificerade utbildare/l&#xE4;rare med l&#xE4;mplig bakgrund och har svag koppling till mediebranschen och nyhetsrapportering. Tack vare insatsen kommer ett regionalt n&#xE4;tverk att etableras och fungera som en mekanism f&#xF6;r gemensamt l&#xE4;rande. N&#xE4;tverksmedlemmarna ska erbjuda systematiska och h&#xF6;gkvalitativa utbildningar till medias akt&#xF6;rer i regionen f&#xF6;r att bem&#xF6;ta aktuella behov i medieindustrin. Detta ska p&#xE5; l&#xE5;ng sikt bidra till en professionaliserad mediesektor som st&#xF6;djer oberoende media, yttrande- och tryckfrihet och r&#xE4;tten till information.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal is to contribute to a professional and independent media sector in Southeast Asia by establishing a regional network of journalism training institutions supporting media freedom, freedom of expression and the right to information. The specific objective is to strengthen the capacity of mid-career journalism training institutes in a regional network covering initially Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam (CLMV countries).</narrative>
  </description>
